// Generated from input/maps-source/map-diagnostic-report-diabetes.csv - do not edit, regenerate with:
//   python scripts/csv2conceptmap.py input/maps-source/map-diagnostic-report-diabetes.csv --source BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes --target be-diagnostic-report-diabetes --title 'Diabetes Report Model to BeDiagnosticReportDiabetes Mapping'
Instance: map-diagnostic-report-diabetes
InstanceOf: ConceptMap
Usage: #definition
Title: "Diabetes Report Model to BeDiagnosticReportDiabetes Mapping"
Description: "Mapping from the BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes logical model to the be-diagnostic-report-diabetes profile"
* url = "https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/glucose-monitoring/ConceptMap/map-diagnostic-report-diabetes"
* name = "MapDiagnosticReportDiabetes"
* status = #draft
* experimental = false

* group[+]
  * source = "https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/glucose-monitoring/StructureDefinition/BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes"
  * target = "https://www.ehealth.fgov.be/standards/fhir/glucose-monitoring/StructureDefinition/be-diagnostic-report-diabetes"
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.businessIdentifier, Business identifier of the report, DiagnosticReport.identifier, Business identifier for report, equivalent, At least one identifier is required\, including the UUID slice with system fixed to be-ns-diagnostic-report-diabetes. Slicing is open\, so other business identifiers can be added.)
  * insert ConceptMapElement(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.recordedDate, Date of the last update of the report, DiagnosticReport.extension:recorded-date, BeExtRecordedDate, equivalent)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.observationPeriod, From date to date corresponding to the period covered by the report. Typically 14 to 30 days. See business rules, DiagnosticReport.effective[x], Clinically relevant time/time-period for report, equivalent, effective[x] is restricted to Period; start and end are both mandatory.)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.patient, The patient that this report is about, DiagnosticReport.subject, The subject of the report - usually\, but not always\, the patient, equivalent, Reference(BePatient\). For GDPR reasons\, sensor suppliers may not use the NISS of their users in external communication.)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.status, Report status\, by default “Final”. The value is assigned according to the business rule on “% Data Captured”, DiagnosticReport.status, registered | partial | preliminary | final +, equivalent, Bound to BeVSDiabetesReportStatus. The value is assigned according to the business rule on % Data Captured.)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.recorder, The healthcare professional (INAMI number / national register number\) or organization (INAMI approval number / company number\) that encodes the information and takes responsibility for its content, DiagnosticReport.extension:recorder, BeExtRecorder, equivalent, Reference(BePractitioner | BeOrganization\). The professional is identified by INAMI or national register number\, the organization by INAMI approval or company number.)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.interpreter, Healthcare provider (INAMI number / national register number\) who added an interpretation to the report (e.g. endocrinologist\, general practitioner\). Not provided by the producer of the report, DiagnosticReport.resultsInterpreter, Primary result interpreter, equivalent, Reference(BePractitionerRole | BePractitioner\). Not provided by the report producer; added by the interpreting care provider.)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.category, Category of the report. At least one category must be assigned, DiagnosticReport.category, Service category, equivalent, Bound (preferred\) to BeVSDiabetesReportCategory.)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.deviceType, Identification number assigned by INAMI to the type of sensor model used to create the observations on which the report is based. The individual sensor device is mentioned in the measurement observation, DiagnosticReport.extension:device, Device Type, equivalent, valueCodeableConcept bound (extensible\) to BeVSDiabetesDeviceType. The individual sensor device is mentioned in the measurement observation.)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.code, Report code - indicating the type of procedure that leads to the production of the primary values of this report\, i.e. 439926003 | Ambulatory continuous glucose monitoring of interstitial tissue fluid, DiagnosticReport.code, Name/Code for this diagnostic report, equivalent, Bound to BeVSDiabetesReportCode (e.g. 439926003 Ambulatory continuous glucose monitoring of interstitial tissue fluid\).)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.derivedObservations, List of references to “derived values” type observations (a dozen derived observations\) mentioned in the report. These observations are part of the diagnostic report, DiagnosticReport.result, Observations, equivalent, Reference(BeObservationDiabetes\).)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.measuredDiabetesObservations, References to the measured diabetes observations (a few thousand measurements\) used to produce the analysis, DiagnosticReport.result, Observations, equivalent, Reference(BeObservationDiabetes\). Shares DiagnosticReport.result with the derived observations; there is no separate slice yet.)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.note, Report comments in free text format. Not provided by the producer of the report\, but by the healthcare provider doing the interpretation, DiagnosticReport.extension:note, BeExtSimpleNote, equivalent, Not provided by the report producer; added by the interpreting care provider.)
  * insert ConceptMapElementWithComment(BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.document, PDF document containing the complete report (text\, graphics\, deduced observations\, conclusions\, etc.\), DiagnosticReport.presentedForm, Entire report as issued, equivalent, contentType fixed to application/pdf.)
